<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements embedded by the CI workflow (.github/workflows/build.yml) when it fake-signs the app
  with ldid. This is the single place to edit them. No Apple account, certificate or provisioning
  profile is involved, so only entitlements that a fake-signing installer honours are useful here.

  The set is intentionally MINIMAL. Every key you add is baked into the IPA, and some installers
  reject IPAs that carry entitlements they do not recognise.

  Keys:
    get-task-allowed (true)
        Standard "debuggable app" entitlement. It allows a debugger or inspection tool to attach
        to the running process (task port), as Xcode adds to development builds. It does not change
        what the app does.

  Deliberately NOT here:
    com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit
    com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing
        Memory entitlements. They are applied by the user after installation with iRAM+, not by
        this build. The workflow fails the build if either one shows up in the signed binary, so
        iRAM+ stays the only place that grants them.
    com.nyxian.pe.*
        Nyxian runtime entitlements (Config/Entitlements.plist). They only mean something inside
        Nyxian and are not part of this build.

  The workflow converts this file with plutil before signing, so these comments are dropped.
  After signing it prints the embedded entitlements (ldid -e) in the job log.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>get-task-allowed</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
